  "findings": [
    {
      "criterion": "natural_arena_pressure",
      "fact": "Contract 33 leaves the exact mechanic, timing and escalation UNKNOWN. Accepted packaged pressure evidence invokes the authoritative API from fixtures. Native ApplyArenaPressure explicitly adds no elapsed-time escalation.",
      "decision": "Do not invent a timer or connect the service-bay switch to the arena-pressure API. Package-04 ordinary input proves power, panel destruction and electrical-floor damage. Package-07 reuses package-06 native code and geometry, and passes the installed environment fixture, but its raw runs record none of those environment events. Keep outcomes bound to the package actually run."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "continuous_600_1200_seconds",
      "fact": "Native objective success and player defeat terminate normal control. Package-07 raw runs terminate at 22.60887735610595 and 9.010236388945486 active seconds. Package-04 ordinary hazard proof lasted 46.3133 seconds; the longest preserved interaction attempt lasted 57.1384 seconds before rival-fire defeat. None qualifies the 600\u20131200 second route.",
      "decision": "Preserve accepted terminal behavior. A supported continuous content sequence is not yet established; restart stitching and idle padding remain prohibited.",
      "causal_evidence": "BiellaOpenWorldGameMode inherits SpawnDemoActors and the two-target Demo objective. BiellaDemoObjectiveManager excludes streaming infected. In hud-1080-01 telemetry the rival alone kills both tracked infected by 9.3066 s; Success follows at 9.4109 s even while streamed population survives. This identifies the early terminal cause without changing accepted behavior.",
      "additional_probe": {
        "run": "raw/route-rival-01",
        "input_plan": "rival-intercept-input.json",
        "package": "preserved D08 Linux installed package; no native overlay",
        "active_simulation_seconds": 14.007807950431015,
        "terminal": "Success",
        "player_weapon_events": 3,
        "observed": "Normal sprint/fire input hits a streaming infected and the first objective infected, not the rival. Population infected then join the target set (target rises from 2 to 6 before success). Rival fire clears the remaining target set. This corrects any inference that all later population is excluded from objective counting; BiellaStreamingInfected and BiellaPopulationInfected have different registration behavior.",
